 {"question":"Which description applies to the intercellular substance (matrix)?","choices":["A transparent, homogeneous material with a definite shape.","A transparent, homogeneous material with no definite shape.","A granular material with a definite shape.","A granular material with no definite shape."],"answer_index":1},
 {"question":"Which consistencies may the intercellular substance have?","choices":["Liquid or semiliquid only.","Gelatinous or solid only.","Liquid or gelatinous only.","Liquid, semiliquid, gelatinous, or solid."],"answer_index":3},
 {"question":"What is the function of the intercellular matrix?","choices":["Occupies spaces between cells and fibers.","Forms all types of connective-tissue fibers.","Joins cell margins by plasma junctions.","Forms antibodies that protect the body."],"answer_index":0},
 {"question":"Connective tissues are classified according to:","choices":["number of cell rows and shape of the superficial layer.","fiber density and fresh color.","cell types and physical properties of the intercellular substance.","shape and position of nuclei."],"answer_index":2},
