 {"question":"On what basis is connective tissue proper classified as loose or dense?","choices":["Shape of superficial cells.","Physical properties of the matrix alone.","Cell location and nuclear shape.","Density of its cellular and fibrous contents."],"answer_index":3},
 {"question":"Which group includes types of loose connective tissue?","choices":["Areolar, adipose, mesenchymal, reticular, and mucous.","Areolar, adipose, mesenchymal, dense, and mucous.","Areolar, adipose, proper, reticular, and mucous.","Areolar, mesenchymal, specialized, reticular, and dense."],"answer_index":0},
 {"question":"Which description distinguishes areolar connective tissue?","choices":["Adipose cells predominate and other cells are few.","Unspecialized cells appear in a liquid matrix.","All fiber types occur at varying densities, along with most connective-tissue cell types.","Closely packed cells with almost no matrix."],"answer_index":2},
 {"question":"Why is areolar connective tissue the most common connective tissue?","choices":["It occurs in early embryonic stages.","It occurs beneath the skin and between different body organs.","It occurs only at fat-storage and metabolic sites.","It occurs in blood-vessel linings."],"answer_index":1},
 {"question":"What is the function of areolar connective tissue?","choices":["Stores fat for energy and protects against heat loss.","Differentiates to form specialized tissues.","Forms antibodies against infection.","Envelops most body structures, including blood and lymphatic vessels and nerves."],"answer_index":3},
 {"question":"Which comparison between areolar and adipose connective tissue is correct?","choices":["Most connective-cell types occur in areolar tissue; adipose cells predominate in adipose tissue.","Adipose cells predominate in areolar tissue; most connective-cell types occur in adipose tissue.","Areolar tissue is embryonic and unspecialized; adipose tissue surrounds nerves.","Areolar tissue stores fat; adipose tissue differentiates into specialized tissues."],"answer_index":0},
 {"question":"Which adipose-tissue location–function pairing is correct?","choices":["Between organs — envelops blood and lymphatic vessels and nerves.","Early embryonic stages — forms specialized tissues.","Under the skin and at fat-storage and metabolic sites — stores fat for energy and protects against heat loss.","Under the skin — forms all connective-tissue fibers."],"answer_index":2},
 {"question":"Which description applies to mesenchymal connective tissue?","choices":["Specialized tissue with cells in a liquid matrix.","Unspecialized tissue with cells in a liquid matrix.","Unspecialized tissue with cells in a solid matrix.","Specialized tissue with cells in a gelatinous matrix."],"answer_index":1},
 {"question":"When is mesenchymal connective tissue present, and what is its fate?","choices":["In adults, then changes into unspecialized embryonic tissue.","Under the skin, then specializes only in fat storage.","Between organs, then specializes only in enveloping nerves.","In early embryonic stages, then differentiates into other adult tissue types."],"answer_index":3},
 {"question":"Which tissue–function pairing is correct?","choices":["Mesenchymal connective tissue — differentiates to form specialized body tissues.","Mesenchymal connective tissue — envelops blood and lymphatic vessels and nerves.","Areolar connective tissue — stores fat for energy.","Adipose connective tissue — differentiates to form specialized body tissues."],"answer_index":0}
